1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,124
This company makes ₩60 trillion in three months,

2
00:00:02,144 --> 00:00:05,280
but the Warren Buffett method puts it at just ₩295,000

3
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:08,218
Less than a quarter of today's ₩1.22 million price

4
00:00:08,238 --> 00:00:10,863
It beat last year's full-year profit in just three months

5
00:00:10,883 --> 00:00:13,025
So why does it come out so cheap?

6
00:00:13,045 --> 00:00:15,166
Memory company profits are a roller coaster

7
00:00:15,186 --> 00:00:19,817
In 2019, 87% of profit vanished, and 2023 was an outright loss

8
00:00:19,837 --> 00:00:23,474
So instead of the peak, you look at the average of good and bad years

9
00:00:23,494 --> 00:00:26,939
That average profit is about 13% of today's profit

10
00:00:26,959 --> 00:00:27,976
Multiply it by 10

11
00:00:27,996 --> 00:00:30,275
and you get ₩295,000

12
00:00:30,295 --> 00:00:34,435
On recent profit, the stock trades at 5.4x earnings. A bargain, right?

13
00:00:34,455 --> 00:00:37,276
But on average profit, it's 41x

14
00:00:37,296 --> 00:00:42,154
So today's price is a bet that profit stays above half even after the boom

15
00:00:42,174 --> 00:00:44,619
After the last two booms, that didn't happen

16
00:00:44,639 --> 00:00:47,636
Will it really be different this time? We dug into it in the full video

